    "## Data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Data overview\n",
    "\n",
    "### Online Shoppers Purchasing Intention Dataset (Real World Data)\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Dataset Name:** Online Shoppers Purchasing Intention Dataset (Real world data)\n",
    "- **Link to the dataset:** https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/468/online+shoppers+purchasing+intention+dataset\n",
    "- **Number of observations:** 12,330 sessions\n",
    "- **Number of variables:** 18 variables\n",
    "\n",
    "**Data Description**\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset used in this project is the Online Shoppers Purchasing Intention Dataset obtained from the UCI Machine Learning Repository.\n",
    "It contains 12,330 observations, where each row represents a single user session on an e-commerce website.\n",
    "The dataset includes 18 variables that describe browsing behavior, session context, and whether the session resulted in a purchase (Revenue).\n",
    "Because the data is session-level rather than user-level, each observation reflects one visit to the website rather than long-term customer behavior.\n",
    "\n",
    "The most important metrics in this dataset relate to browsing engagement and purchase intent. Page visit variables such as Administrative, Informational, and ProductRelated measure the number of pages viewed in each category (unit: page counts).\n",
    "Corresponding duration variables (e.g., ProductRelated_Duration) measure time spent on those pages in seconds.\n",
    "BounceRates and ExitRates are proportions between 0 and 1 that represent the likelihood of leaving the website after viewing a page; values closer to 1 indicate higher likelihood of exiting.\n",
    "PageValues represents the estimated monetary value of a page based on historical transaction data, with higher values suggesting stronger purchase intent.\n",
    "SpecialDay ranges from 0 to 1 and represents how close the session occurred to a special shopping day (e.g., holidays), where values closer to 1 indicate proximity to that event.\n",
    "The target variable, Revenue, is binary (1 = purchase occurred, 0 = no purchase).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Data Relevance to the Research Question\n",
    "This dataset is directly relevant to our research question because it contains both the independent variables and the outcome variable needed to examine purchasing behavior.\n",
    "Our research question asks which combinations of browsing engagement features and session context variables are associated with the highest probability of generating revenue.\n",
    "The dataset includes detailed engagement metrics such as ProductRelated page visits, time spent on pages, informational and administrative interactions, and PageValues, which together capture user interest and purchase intent.\n",
    "In addition, the dataset includes contextual variables such as Month, Weekend, SpecialDay, TrafficType, and VisitorType. These variables allow us to analyze how purchasing behavior changes across different shopping occasions and traffic sources.\n",
    "Most importantly, the dataset includes a binary Revenue variable indicating whether a purchase occurred. Because both predictors (engagement + context) and the outcome (purchase) are present in the same structured dataset, it enables direct analysis of how combinations of behavioral and contextual factors relate to conversion probability.\n",
    "Although the data comes from a single e-commerce platform and is session-based rather than user-based, it provides sufficient behavioral granularity to meaningfully investigate patterns in online purchasing behavior. Therefore, it is well aligned with the goals of this project.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Data Shortcomings\n",
    "One potential concern with this dataset is that it originates from a single e-commerce platform, meaning results may not generalize to all online shopping environments.\n",
    "Additionally, the dataset is session-based rather than customer-based, so repeat visitors may appear multiple times without being explicitly linked across sessions.\n",
    "The dataset is also class imbalanced, with only about 15% of sessions resulting in a purchase, which may influence predictive modeling performance.\n",
    "Finally, contextual variables such as income level, product type, and marketing campaigns are not included, limiting causal interpretation.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Variables Most Relevant to the Research Question\n",
    "\n",
    "**Browsing Engagement Metrics**\n",
    "\n",
    "- **ProductRelated:** number of product pages viewed\n",
    "- **ProductRelated_Duration:** time spent on product pages (seconds)\n",
    "- **Informational:** number of informational pages viewed\n",
    "- **Administrative:** number of administrative pages viewed\n",
    "- **PageValues:** estimated value of web pages visited (purchase intent proxy)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Session Context Variables**\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Month:** month in which the session occurred\n",
    "- **Weekend:** whether the session occurred on a weekend (0 = No, 1 = Yes)\n",
    "- **SpecialDay:** proximity to a holiday (range 0–1)\n",
    "- **TrafficType:** traffic source category\n",
    "- **VisitorType:** returning vs new visitor\n",
    "\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
