    "This plot compares the number of sessions that resulted in purchases versus those that did not across different months. Across all months, sessions that did not result in revenue significantly outnumber those that did. However, some months show noticeably higher numbers of purchase sessions than others. In particular, November has the highest number of purchase sessions, followed by May and December. This pattern suggests that purchasing behavior may be influenced by seasonal shopping periods, as November and December typically correspond to major online shopping events and holiday sales. These results indicate that certain months may be associated with increased purchasing activity compared to others."
