    "Results:\n",
    "\n",
    "The logistic regression results show that PageValues has the strongest positive coefficient, indicating that sessions involving pages with higher estimated transaction value are much more likely to result in a purchase. In contrast, ExitRates has a strong negative coefficient, suggesting that sessions where users frequently leave pages are less likely to generate revenue. BounceRates also shows a negative relationship with purchases, indicating that sessions with quick exits tend to have lower conversion probability.\n",
    "\n",
    "Some contextual variables also appear among the influential features. Month_Nov has a positive coefficient, indicating that sessions occurring in November are associated with a higher likelihood of purchase compared to the baseline month. Several other month indicators show smaller effects, suggesting that seasonal timing can influence purchasing behavior. Additionally, certain traffic source variables (such as TrafficType_13 and TrafficType_15) appear among the top features, indicating that the source of website traffic can affect purchase probability."
